# **`COPY . .` copies whatever is in the working tree, and `.gitignore` does not
# apply to it.** Without this file the build copied the host's `node_modules`
# over the `linux-musl` tree `npm ci` had just installed — on a Windows
# workstation that means win32 binaries and `.bin` shims in a Linux image — and
# dragged 96 MB of `out/` into the build context for no reason. It also made the
# build non-hermetic: the result depended on what the host happened to be
# carrying, including an `.env` that Git ignores and Docker does not.

.git
.gitignore
.github

node_modules
.next
.source
.sources
out

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
